WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:12.640
MINH NGUYEN: Hi.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:14.970
And welcome to "The future
of application development

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:16.950
with cloud databases."

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:17.910
My name is Minh.

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:21.330
And I'm a product manager
for Cloud Firestore.

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:27.384
Join with me today and Natan,
a software engineer from Dott.

00:00:27.384 --> 00:00:33.260
Today's session will be focused
on resolving one key question--

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:38.090
why is it so challenging to
build and scale applications?

00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:40.340
And more importantly,
what is Google

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:42.710
doing to make application
development easier?

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.860
To answer this
question, we'll begin

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:52.610
by reviewing two popular
application architectures.

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:55.580
Choosing an architecture
has a large impact

00:00:55.580 --> 00:01:00.480
on how an application is
built and how it scales.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:02.500
In the second part
of the session,

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:04.080
you'll hear a
customer testimonial

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:07.530
from Dott describing how
thoughtful architectural

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:11.160
decisions have impacted
their business.

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:14.040
Finally, we'll round out
the session with new product

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:18.255
announcements and resources
to learn more about Firestore.

00:01:18.255 --> 00:01:19.005
Let's get started.

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:25.720
Imagine for a moment that
you're writing a new application

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:28.750
and decide to use a
more traditional n-tier

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:30.780
architecture.

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:35.100
Today's example can apply to
any general purpose application,

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:37.110
but to ground the
discussion let's

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:40.430
assume it's an e-commerce app.

00:01:40.430 --> 00:01:43.670
At the heart of the
application is a database.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:46.280
The database is
used to store data.

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:50.920
In front of the
database are typically

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:53.800
a set of microservices that
manage your application's

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:55.750
business logic.

00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:58.840
Let's assume that you have
three separate microservices--

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:00.880
a service for your
product catalog,

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:04.365
a service for your product
inventory, and lastly a service

00:02:04.365 --> 00:02:05.365
for your shopping carts.

00:02:08.949 --> 00:02:12.670
As usage for your microservices
grow and declines,

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:14.470
you'll need to load
balance traffic

00:02:14.470 --> 00:02:17.800
while horizontally scaling
and compacting capacity.

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:23.210
In order to secure access
to these microservices,

00:02:23.210 --> 00:02:24.890
you'll need to add
an API gateway.

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:31.020
Finally, to enable
broad distribution

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:33.690
of your application, you'll
need to develop clients--

00:02:33.690 --> 00:02:39.170
the web, Android, and even iOS.

00:02:39.170 --> 00:02:42.050
Furthermore, you want to make
sure that your users always

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:43.880
have the latest data.

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:46.400
To access your application
when they're offline,

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.650
you'll need to add
support for web sockets

00:02:48.650 --> 00:02:51.820
and an offline caching system.

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:55.150
As you can see, there's a lot
of technical complexity here.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:01.780
Unfortunately
technical complexity

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:06.010
can be the enemy of
business innovation.

00:03:06.010 --> 00:03:09.595
Let's examine the downstream
impact this architecture has.

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:15.890
First, operationalizing
all the services

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:20.260
that support an application
can be intensive.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:23.170
Second, each layer
of the architecture

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:26.620
typically represents
specialized teams,

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:28.720
which means complex
dependency planning

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:31.720
and therefore potential
risks for project delay.

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:38.670
Third, sourcing talent for
each layer of the architecture

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:42.750
can be difficult and
expensive, especially

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:46.590
in competitive hiring
markets like today.

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:48.380
Let's figure out how
Google is solving

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:50.450
for each of these
challenges, starting

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:51.860
with the operational challenge.

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:57.410
Google offers
management services

00:03:57.410 --> 00:03:59.850
for each layer of the stack.

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:03.030
With Cloud SQL, for
example, we will assist you

00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:06.750
in operationalizing popular
relational databases

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:11.835
such as PostgreSQL, MySQL,
or even Microsoft SQL.

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:16.779
With Kubernetes Engine,
we will assist you

00:04:16.779 --> 00:04:21.620
in operationalizing
your microservices.

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:25.230
With Apigee, we will assist you
in operationalizing your API

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:25.730
gateway.

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:33.170
So the combination of these
management services from Google

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:35.390
will assist you in
operationalizing

00:04:35.390 --> 00:04:38.240
each layer in the stack
while still enabling

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:41.640
high customization.

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:44.100
Alternatively, if you're
interested in taking

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:47.550
the surplus route,
you can use Cloud Run

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:52.260
to run your microservices in
Firestore as your database.

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:56.860
Choosing to go the
serverless route

00:04:56.860 --> 00:04:59.830
allows you to delegate
operational complexity

00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:02.980
to Google, freeing
up your team to focus

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:06.880
on product development.

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:07.930
OK.

00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:10.300
We've addressed
operational complexity,

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:14.200
but what about projects
or hiring complexity?

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:17.290
Let's examine how a deeper
investment in Firestore

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:19.240
can address the
remaining challenges.

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:25.820
Firestore is a serverless
document database

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:30.830
that can also act as a
complete backend as a service.

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:33.680
Firebase Auth is a
service that allows

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:36.500
you to delegate your
applications auth and user

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:39.236
management to Google.

00:05:39.236 --> 00:05:43.170
Firestore and Firebase Auth
are seamlessly integrated.

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:45.600
Using a combination
of these two services

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:48.660
allows customers to
focus on UI development,

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:52.410
delegating secure auth and
backend service management

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:54.820
to Google.

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:57.250
Furthermore, you'll get
built-in functionality

00:05:57.250 --> 00:06:00.310
for real-time synchronization,
connection management

00:06:00.310 --> 00:06:03.760
between clients
and your database,

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:06.790
and offline caching
using the Firestore SDKs.

00:06:10.780 --> 00:06:13.500
So by using Firestore as
a backend of the service,

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:15.810
you can focus on UI development.

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:19.560
And UI teams are empowered
to make decisions,

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:23.235
as they no longer are dependent
on changes from backend teams.

00:06:26.950 --> 00:06:29.200
With universal
application frameworks

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:31.900
like Google Flutter
or Facebook React,

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:33.880
you can now write
native applications

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:36.490
using a single code
base and deploy them

00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:40.570
across multiple client platforms
such as the web, Android,

00:06:40.570 --> 00:06:42.930
and iOS.

00:06:42.930 --> 00:06:47.310
Firestore fully supports
these universal app frameworks

00:06:47.310 --> 00:06:50.130
with an easy-to-use
set of plain SDKs.

00:06:53.710 --> 00:06:57.490
As a result, with Firestore
and universal app frameworks

00:06:57.490 --> 00:07:00.910
you can focus on hiring
for Flutter or React skills

00:07:00.910 --> 00:07:03.610
from a very large
pool of developers.

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:08.110
The result of these
investments enables

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:10.810
you to focus on
business innovation

00:07:10.810 --> 00:07:14.395
through a single autonomous
team and code base.

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:21.540
There are many factors that go
into application development.

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:24.750
And at Google, we're investing
in a complete ecosystem

00:07:24.750 --> 00:07:26.400
for app development.

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:31.020
This includes, one, core
UI frameworks and operating

00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:34.810
systems to build
applications, two,

00:07:34.810 --> 00:07:38.650
in-app services from Firebase
to manage aspects like auth,

00:07:38.650 --> 00:07:42.220
and three, backend
services from Google Cloud

00:07:42.220 --> 00:07:44.980
to manage aspects like
back office analytics using

00:07:44.980 --> 00:07:47.020
BigQuery.

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:50.710
Firestore brings together
these portfolio investments

00:07:50.710 --> 00:07:54.130
in an intelligent way by
enabling seamless integration

00:07:54.130 --> 00:07:56.440
into each of these portfolios.

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:03.030
Frequently applications rely
on third-party services,

00:08:03.030 --> 00:08:06.330
and it's important that these
services are also seamlessly

00:08:06.330 --> 00:08:09.370
integrated with Firestore.

00:08:09.370 --> 00:08:11.860
One popular integration
request we've received

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:15.240
has been an integration
with Elastic.

00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:18.750
Today, we're excited to
announce, in partnership

00:08:18.750 --> 00:08:21.510
with Elastic, a
new extension that

00:08:21.510 --> 00:08:23.940
streams changes from
a Firestore database

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:27.320
to an Elastic app
search instance.

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:30.340
You can install this extension
and many other third-party

00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:33.220
extensions from the Firebase
extensions directory.

00:08:36.059 --> 00:08:39.020
So in summary, Firestore
allows customers

00:08:39.020 --> 00:08:42.830
to focus on business value
and product differentiation.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:46.070
[INAUDIBLE] document database
that can also act as a backend

00:08:46.070 --> 00:08:48.330
to service.

00:08:48.330 --> 00:08:52.350
With over 250,000 monthly
active developers,

00:08:52.350 --> 00:08:55.560
you can have confidence
that the solution

00:08:55.560 --> 00:09:00.710
is backed by a large
community of developers.

00:09:00.710 --> 00:09:03.440
Furthermore, with
Firestore applications now

00:09:03.440 --> 00:09:09.050
supporting 750 million monthly
active end users using Firebase

00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:12.110
Auth, you can be confident
that Firestore will

00:09:12.110 --> 00:09:13.925
scale to your business's needs.

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:20.890
We've covered the
traditional n-tier

00:09:20.890 --> 00:09:23.030
in Firestore architectures.

00:09:23.030 --> 00:09:25.150
Let's review the
strengths of each.

00:09:27.880 --> 00:09:31.270
The traditional n-tier
offers a high customizability

00:09:31.270 --> 00:09:34.060
and is compatible with
popular open source frameworks

00:09:34.060 --> 00:09:35.900
and libraries.

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:38.200
However, as we explained
in this session,

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:41.500
this normally comes at the
trade-off of technical,

00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:45.670
project, and hiring complexity.

00:09:45.670 --> 00:09:47.590
Pricing for this
solution is often

00:09:47.590 --> 00:09:49.690
driven by a capacity
model, which

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:52.870
means that you have to configure
how capacity is scaled,

00:09:52.870 --> 00:09:55.180
and you're billed for
capacity even when

00:09:55.180 --> 00:09:56.530
it's not fully utilized.

00:09:59.670 --> 00:10:03.090
Firestore, on the other hand,
provides a fully integrated,

00:10:03.090 --> 00:10:05.730
Google-based solution
that significantly

00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:12.800
reduces technical, operational,
project, and hiring complexity.

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:15.290
Customers who choose
Firestore have the flexibility

00:10:15.290 --> 00:10:18.710
to use it as a
backend of a service,

00:10:18.710 --> 00:10:24.190
in an n-tier architecture, or
maybe a hybrid of the both.

00:10:24.190 --> 00:10:26.800
Since it's serverless,
pricing for Firestore

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:30.340
is based on the actual
operations conducted, storage

00:10:30.340 --> 00:10:33.680
used, or network egress.

00:10:33.680 --> 00:10:36.920
And with that I'm excited
to introduce Natan

00:10:36.920 --> 00:10:41.458
from Dott, who will share
how Dott uses Firestore.

00:10:41.458 --> 00:10:44.846
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:10:54.050 --> 00:10:55.340
NATAN SAGOL: Good morning.

00:10:55.340 --> 00:10:57.920
I'm Natan, one of
the engineers who

00:10:57.920 --> 00:11:01.640
joined Dott at the very
beginning of our journey.

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:05.960
We are a micromobility operator
with over 50,000 e-scooters

00:11:05.960 --> 00:11:10.740
and e-bikes across
45 cities in Europe.

00:11:10.740 --> 00:11:15.030
We are active in nine countries,
in capitals like London, Paris,

00:11:15.030 --> 00:11:19.460
and Warsaw, and
many more cities.

00:11:19.460 --> 00:11:21.410
I have been fortunate
to participate

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:24.590
in growing our company
from the very first scooter

00:11:24.590 --> 00:11:28.110
to tens of thousands
we operate today,

00:11:28.110 --> 00:11:31.620
to see our engineering
organization expand to over 30

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:32.580
people--

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:34.650
looking forward to
welcoming many more

00:11:34.650 --> 00:11:37.380
before the year's end--

00:11:37.380 --> 00:11:39.840
to enable millions
to take clean rights.

00:11:42.520 --> 00:11:45.950
At Dott, we deeply care
about the environment,

00:11:45.950 --> 00:11:51.080
and we try to reduce our carbon
footprint as much as possible.

00:11:51.080 --> 00:11:53.540
While Google Cloud
is carbon neutral,

00:11:53.540 --> 00:11:57.140
it's even better not to
consume any kind of resources

00:11:57.140 --> 00:11:59.770
in the first place.

00:11:59.770 --> 00:12:01.290
That's why we
choose technologies

00:12:01.290 --> 00:12:07.450
which rapidly up and downscale
to precisely match our needs.

00:12:07.450 --> 00:12:11.220
Firestore is one of
these technologies.

00:12:11.220 --> 00:12:13.350
It has been a core
to our solutions

00:12:13.350 --> 00:12:16.350
from the very beginning.

00:12:16.350 --> 00:12:20.490
We started on Firestore by
connecting our vehicles, which

00:12:20.490 --> 00:12:23.700
frequently send information
about their location

00:12:23.700 --> 00:12:27.460
and relevant telemetry.

00:12:27.460 --> 00:12:30.250
We quickly moved to
user-facing features,

00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:33.930
using Firestore as a backend.

00:12:33.930 --> 00:12:36.720
Connecting to it
directly from our apps

00:12:36.720 --> 00:12:41.200
allowed us to work
efficiently and independently.

00:12:41.200 --> 00:12:43.630
We were a small team back then.

00:12:43.630 --> 00:12:46.720
Removing the need for
any backend development

00:12:46.720 --> 00:12:50.060
allowed us to shift
features quickly.

00:12:50.060 --> 00:12:53.840
In a single day with
real-time synchronization,

00:12:53.840 --> 00:12:57.110
we were able to implement
a vibrant live map

00:12:57.110 --> 00:12:58.160
of available scooters.

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:04.210
Over time, we added
many functionalities,

00:13:04.210 --> 00:13:06.820
from basic ones like
starting and ending

00:13:06.820 --> 00:13:11.590
a trip to more complex, such
as payment processing, where

00:13:11.590 --> 00:13:14.750
accuracy is critical.

00:13:14.750 --> 00:13:17.210
For these
functionalities, Firestore

00:13:17.210 --> 00:13:21.560
provided us not only with an
ability to develop rapidly,

00:13:21.560 --> 00:13:25.130
but with an ability to
develop with confidence,

00:13:25.130 --> 00:13:27.230
allowing us to
ensure correctness

00:13:27.230 --> 00:13:28.820
with the use of transactions.

00:13:31.750 --> 00:13:34.040
The world changes all the time.

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:36.620
So does our business.

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:38.810
More sophisticated
functionalities

00:13:38.810 --> 00:13:42.290
require specialized services.

00:13:42.290 --> 00:13:44.300
We have developed
a lot of these,

00:13:44.300 --> 00:13:48.395
and each time Firestore has
proven to be a good fit.

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:55.340
Some of these services replaced
directories from our apps

00:13:55.340 --> 00:13:58.280
when we needed complexity
that was easier to manage

00:13:58.280 --> 00:14:01.110
with a dedicated backend.

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:02.820
But we are grateful
we didn't have

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:06.150
to implement all of
this back in the days

00:14:06.150 --> 00:14:07.830
when there were
just a few of us.

00:14:10.430 --> 00:14:13.550
Some of the recent
changes we all experienced

00:14:13.550 --> 00:14:18.540
were challenging for individuals
and businesses alike.

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:21.960
Shelter-in-place
orders, while necessary,

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:27.310
affected every one of us and
affected a lot of companies,

00:14:27.310 --> 00:14:30.828
including Dott.

00:14:30.828 --> 00:14:35.410
Our choice to utilize Firestore
and our serverless products

00:14:35.410 --> 00:14:38.590
helped us navigate
shelter in place.

00:14:38.590 --> 00:14:42.760
With the lower usage came a
lower bill with the expected

00:14:42.760 --> 00:14:46.470
one-to-one correlation.

00:14:46.470 --> 00:14:50.850
Nowadays many lean more towards
individual transportation,

00:14:50.850 --> 00:14:54.330
such as with the use of
e-scooters and e-bikes

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:57.480
due to health safety reasons.

00:14:57.480 --> 00:15:01.620
At Dott, we see many more
riders and trips in comparison

00:15:01.620 --> 00:15:05.460
to pre-COVID numbers, with
utilization of our fleet

00:15:05.460 --> 00:15:11.600
75% higher in some
cities such as Brussels.

00:15:11.600 --> 00:15:14.330
Scalability of
Firestore enabled us

00:15:14.330 --> 00:15:17.090
to support this demand
without requiring

00:15:17.090 --> 00:15:18.635
any changes on our side.

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:24.740
As regard to our
infrastructure, we simply

00:15:24.740 --> 00:15:27.700
don't have to worry
what happens next.

00:15:27.700 --> 00:15:29.980
Firestore will
adapt to our needs

00:15:29.980 --> 00:15:31.690
and support us in our journey.

00:15:34.680 --> 00:15:37.890
Now that you know a bit
more about our history,

00:15:37.890 --> 00:15:39.990
it's a good time to
share with you what

00:15:39.990 --> 00:15:43.730
I think about it in retrospect.

00:15:43.730 --> 00:15:47.390
While at the beginning we were
considering other databases--

00:15:47.390 --> 00:15:50.930
relational, graph, and
document oriented--

00:15:50.930 --> 00:15:54.320
today I know that we
couldn't have made a better

00:15:54.320 --> 00:15:57.570
choice than Firestore.

00:15:57.570 --> 00:15:59.760
That's why it's such a
pleasure for me to be here

00:15:59.760 --> 00:16:03.500
today and give this testimony.

00:16:03.500 --> 00:16:04.570
Thank you all.

00:16:04.570 --> 00:16:07.930
And thank you, the
Firestore team.

00:16:07.930 --> 00:16:08.890
Back to you, Minh.

