Next, I'll be sharing
exciting product announcements

00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:26.300
for Firestore.

00:16:29.050 --> 00:16:31.630
Firestore is committed to
the security and privacy

00:16:31.630 --> 00:16:33.370
of our customers.

00:16:33.370 --> 00:16:35.380
To demonstrate that
commitment, I'm

00:16:35.380 --> 00:16:39.340
excited to announce
four new features.

00:16:39.340 --> 00:16:43.690
With Data Access Audit Logs,
privileged administrators

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:46.780
will be able to audit
all operations conducted

00:16:46.780 --> 00:16:50.070
on a database.

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:53.730
With custom IAM,
customers will be

00:16:53.730 --> 00:16:55.770
able to align
Firestore permissions

00:16:55.770 --> 00:16:59.700
to their organization's
IAM roles.

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:03.090
You can get started with Data
Access Audit Logs and custom

00:17:03.090 --> 00:17:06.710
IAM today.

00:17:06.710 --> 00:17:09.470
With VPC Service
Controls, customers

00:17:09.470 --> 00:17:12.829
will be able to reduce
exfiltration risk using network

00:17:12.829 --> 00:17:15.980
level security controls.

00:17:15.980 --> 00:17:17.960
And with App Check,
customers will

00:17:17.960 --> 00:17:20.960
be able to ensure only signed
and pre-authorized client

00:17:20.960 --> 00:17:25.150
applications are allowed to
make requests to Firestore.

00:17:25.150 --> 00:17:28.990
Both the previews of VPC
Service Controls and App Check

00:17:28.990 --> 00:17:30.595
will be rolling out in Q4.

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:38.540
Firestore's developer
experience truly sets it apart,

00:17:38.540 --> 00:17:42.810
and we are continually
investing in this area.

00:17:42.810 --> 00:17:45.000
With Key Visualizer,
customers will

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:47.520
be able to quickly
identify performance issues

00:17:47.520 --> 00:17:52.290
with a visual
performance profiling.

00:17:52.290 --> 00:17:55.090
With the latest
version of our Web SDK

00:17:55.090 --> 00:17:57.420
we have added tree
shaking, which

00:17:57.420 --> 00:18:02.430
enables the reduction of the
SDK footprint by as much as 80%.

00:18:02.430 --> 00:18:06.510
That means faster load
times for your application.

00:18:06.510 --> 00:18:09.210
Both Key Visualizer
and the new Web SDK

00:18:09.210 --> 00:18:11.130
are generally available today.

00:18:14.220 --> 00:18:18.270
We'll also be graduating with
Unity and C++ SDKs to general

00:18:18.270 --> 00:18:21.190
availability in Q4.

00:18:21.190 --> 00:18:24.280
Both of these SDKs are
focused on making it easier

00:18:24.280 --> 00:18:27.370
to develop mobile
games using Firestore.

00:18:30.390 --> 00:18:33.720
Lastly, I'm excited to
announce the graduation

00:18:33.720 --> 00:18:37.680
of Cloud Functions Triggering
to general availability.

00:18:37.680 --> 00:18:39.750
Cloud Functions
Triggering enables

00:18:39.750 --> 00:18:43.800
customers to execute custom
business logic in response

00:18:43.800 --> 00:18:46.005
to changes to a
Firestore document.

00:18:49.220 --> 00:18:50.720
This session is
coming to an end,

00:18:50.720 --> 00:18:55.790
but I hope this was just the
beginning of a shared journey.

00:18:55.790 --> 00:18:59.100
If you want to take a moment to
try Firestore out for yourself,

00:18:59.100 --> 00:19:00.870
you can take a peek
at our quick start

00:19:00.870 --> 00:19:06.660
guides, YouTube [INAUDIBLE]
series, and Qwiklabs.

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:09.540
If you have additional
questions about using Firestore,

00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:13.850
we encourage you to post those
questions on Stack Overflow.

00:19:13.850 --> 00:19:14.930
My name was Minh.

00:19:14.930 --> 00:19:17.420
And I hope that you
enjoyed today's session.

00:19:17.420 --> 00:19:19.580
If you did, please take
a moment to fill out

00:19:19.580 --> 00:19:21.610
the follow-up survey.

00:19:21.610 --> 00:19:23.490
Bye for now.

